{
  "raw": {
    "https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/32359": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Position in Sociocultural Anthropology",
      "description": "Pitzer College, Office of the Dean of Faculty Skip to main content AcademicJobsOnline .org ‌ View Jobs Events Registered Employers Contact Us Login Pitzer College, Office of the Dean of Faculty Position ID: Pitzer College-Office of the Dean of Faculty-TTANTH [#32359] Position Title: Tenure Track Position in Sociocultural Anthropology Position Type: Tenured/Tenure-track faculty Position Location: Claremont, California 91711, United States of America [ map ] Subject Area: Anthropology / Sociocultural Appl Deadline: 2026/11/01 23:59:59  (posted 2026/07/23 , listed until 2026/11/01) Position Description: Apply Position Description Tenure Track Position in Sociocultural Anthropology Pitzer College invites applications for a tenure track position in sociocultural anthropology at the assistant professor or advanced assistant professor level specializing in the histories and trajectories of capitalism, colonialism and other global technologies of governance, including those pivotal to realignments in the global order. Research may include, but is not limited to, analysis of racial stratification, dispossession, imperialism, neoliberalism, development, migration, settler colonialism, decolonization, social movements, and resistance. We particularly welcome candidates focusing on South Asia, Africa (outside of West Africa), or Indigenous peoples. The Claremont Colleges currently have anthropologists working in East Asia, Latin America, the Middle East, and the United States, and we are not seeking applicants working in these areas, with the exception of those studying indigeneity in the Americas. The successful candidate should be prepared to teach one or more courses that embed ethnographic analysis within historical approaches. The new faculty member will teach in their areas of specialization and contribute one or more courses required for the Anthropology major (e.g., Introduction to Sociocultural Anthropology, History of Anthropological Theory, or Field Methods in Anthropology) as well as periodically teaching a writing-intensive course in the college’s first-year seminar program. Applicants must have a Ph.D. in Anthropology or be ABD and are expected to have a Ph.D. in Anthropology by the starting time of the appointment. Pitzer College welcomes candidates who can contribute to the College’s mission and distinctive educational objectives, which promote interdisciplinary perspectives, intercultural understanding, and concern with social responsibility and the ethical implications of knowledge and action. Pitzer College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. For the successful applicant with the relevant interests, affiliations are possible with the intercollegiate departments of Africana Studies, Asian American Studies, Chican@/Latin@ Studies, and/or the Intercollegiate Feminist Center for Teaching, Research, and Engagement. Collaborations with the Robert Redford Conservancy for Southern California Sustainability, the Institute for Global-Local Action and Study, the Community Engagement Center, and the CASA Pitzer program are encouraged.\r\n \r\nTo apply, submit a Letter of Application, current curriculum vitae, evidence of excellence in teaching, teaching evaluations, research statement, 1 article length writing sample, and three letters of recommendation. Additionally, candidates should include a separate statement that addresses how their cultural, experiential, and/or academic background has the potential to contribute to the College’s mission, distinctive educational objectives, and core values. Compensation range: $96,000-98,000 The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors,\r\nincluding but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training.\r\nPitzer College is committed to providing comprehensive benefits to eligible employees and their eligible dependents. Our benefits package includes competitive compensation, health, dental, and vision insurance, retirement savings plans, generous paid time off (vacation, holidays, sick time, parental leave, bereavement, etc.), tuition reimbursement, tuition exchange program participation and more. Questions may be directed to faculty_jobs@pitzer.edu. \r\n \r\nApplication Materials Required:\r\nSubmit the following items online at this website to complete your application: https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/32359 . Please note Academic Jobs Online is on Eastern Time. • Letter of Application\r\n• Three letters of Recommendation\r\n• Current Curriculum Vitae\r\n• Teaching statement and Teaching evaluations\r\n• Research statement \r\n• 1 Article length writing sample \r\n• Statement of potential contributions to Pitzer College’s mission, educational objectives, and core values And anything else requested in the position description.\r\nFurther Info: https://www.pitzer.edu/dean-of-faculty/ Faculty Jobs https://www.pitzer.edu/academics 1050 N Mills Avenue\r\nClaremont, CA\r\n91711 Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: Curriculum Vitae Research statement Teaching statement Letter of Application Writing Sample Statement of potential contributions to Pitzer College’s mission, educational objectives, and core values Course evaluations or other evidence of teaching effectiveness Three reference letters (to be submitted online by the reference writers on this site ) And anything else requested in the position description. Further Info: https://www.pitzer.edu/dean-of-faculty/ 1050 N Mills Avenue Claremont, CA 91711 © 2026 AcademicJobsOnline.Org. All Rights Reserved."
    },
